A||N||1||bHooper||Steering rack rebuild||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||10-31-2000||09:52 AM||||Anyone ever done this?  I have ordered a new bushing and bearing from Rodney, and plan to rebuild my steering rack.<P>Any tips on seperating it from the column?<BR>Is it necesary to replace the inner tie rods?  What are the symptoms of a bad inner tie rod?<P>Thanks!<BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||prof bobo||11-01-2000||10:55 AM||||Yep, I've done it.  You'll probably want to look at this thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006487.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006487.html</A>  for info.  It's not particularly hard to do.  Separating it from the column is a piece of cake.  Putting it back in ... have a second person to wiggle the steering wheel while you try to slide it back together, the boot getting in the way was my biggest gripe. <BR>90% of the work involved with replacing the the inner rods is removing the rack, so you should be able to do the math, eh?  Have fun!||||reg||1
